# Vajra — Full Frontend ↔ Backend Integration Plan

## Overview

The backend (FastAPI, port 8000) and frontend (React/Vite, port 5174) are currently **partially connected**. The `/process` and `/permissions` wiring exists but 5 critical flows are broken or missing. This plan closes every gap.

---

## Current Gaps

| # | Gap | Symptom |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **No file upload endpoint** | Frontend sends filenames only — backend never receives file bytes |
| 2 | **No ChromaDB ingest endpoint** | "Add to Database" + Pipeline ingest are purely frontend mock |
| 3 | **No SSE streaming in chat** | Frontend uses blocking `POST /process`; no real-time token stream |
| 4 | **No conversation history** | Each message sent in isolation — model has no memory of prior turns |
| 5 | **No workspace folder ingest** | Local folder path chip is UI-only; backend never reads the folder |
| 6 | **`api.js` incomplete** | Upload, ingest, stream, and history calls are absent |

---

## Architecture After Integration

```
Browser (React)
   │
   ├── POST /upload          → saves files to server temp dir, returns saved paths
   ├── POST /ingest          → ChromaDB indexes uploaded files / workspace path
   ├── POST /process         → runs orchestrator (non-streaming, with history)
   ├── GET  /stream (SSE)    → streams token chunks for chat (replaces /process in chat)
   ├── GET  /permissions/pending
   └── POST /permissions/approve
```

---

## Open Questions / Decisions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Streaming vs. Non-Streaming for Chat**
> The backend already has `POST /stream` (SSE). Should the chat use streaming (tokens appear word-by-word like Claude) or keep the current blocking response? **Recommended: streaming** — this plan implements it via `EventSource`.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **File storage on server**
> Uploaded files need a place to live on the server. Plan uses `VAJRA_WORKSPACE/uploads/` (already in `.env` as `VAJRA_WORKSPACE=C:\Users\HP\Downloads\vajra`). Files are saved there and their absolute paths are passed to the orchestrator.

